{"availability":"available","full":"sfu-db/lineagex","name":"lineagex","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":86,"forks":6,"created":"2023-05-05T03:05:44Z","updated":"2026-08-12T21:27:03Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://zshandy.github.io/lineagex-demo/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:12.711Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:12.711Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:12.711Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T16:06:12.711Z","stars":86,"forks":6}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Have you ever wondered what is the column level relationship among your SQL scripts and base tables? Don't worry, this tool is intended to help you by creating an interactive graph on a webpage to explore the column level lineage among them(Currently only supports Postgres, other connection types or dialects are under development).","A general introduction of the project can be found in this blog post."],"features":["Automatic dependency creation: When there are dependency among the SQL files, and those tables are not yet in the database, LineageX will automatically tries to find the dependency table and creates it.","Clean and simple but very interactive user interface: The user interface is very simple to use with minimal clutters on the page while showing all of the necessary information.","Variety of SQL statements: LineageX supports a variety of SQL statements, aside from the typical SELECT statement, it also supports CREATE TABLE/VIEW [IF NOT EXISTS] statement as well as the INSERT and DELETE statement.","dbt support: LineageX also implemented in the dbt-LineageX, it is added into a dbt project and by using the dbt library fal, it is able to reuse the Python core and create the similar output from the dbt project."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sfu-db/lineagex/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"db35cfbe99b13c3bdc